#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:180
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns the one gate that decides publish or iterate, and is deliberately unspecialised: this process relaxes the paper process's clinical-SME lane into whichever reviewer a given document actually binds, because no single expertise fits every document the way it does a guideline."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:69
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns the one gate this process has that the paper process does not — the profile check — so nothing with a math kind, a lean field or a .lean sibling reaches Task_Validate or Task_Render pretending to be document content; everything downstream of Gateway_ProfileClean assumes that profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:197
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:181
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:203
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_ContributorFeedback: while the document is a working draft, the Authoring Committee gives feedback through the Contributor Feedback sheet, and each change set is edited and merged in its own pull request. When its changes are merged, the document is validated and rendered again (owner, 2026-10-31)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:187
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:162
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ready to publish?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:78
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewer / subject-matter expert"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:137
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Schema and constraint checks over every block."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Scope it: chapters, the blocks each needs, which statements are normative."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:170
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "See draft-to-publication.bpmn for the review and release path this expands into. Release authorisation is not relaxable."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:193
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Task_AuthorBlocks is where every loop in this process lands — a profile violation from Lane_Build and an iterate from Lane_Reviewer both come back here — so this lane, not either gate, is what actually turns a rejection into a fixed block; Task_Scaffold runs once, before either loop exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only place a person acts before the process becomes agent- and pipeline-driven: Task_Plan sets the chapters, the blocks each needs and which statements are normative, once, before Lane_WorkPlan seeds a bean and Lane_Agent takes over every later edit, including every iteration the review and profile-check loops send back."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:84
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The people writing the document with the editor. While it is a working draft they give feedback through the Contributor Feedback sheet, one change set per row, and each row runs Process_ContributorFeedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:154
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer this folio binds. authoring-document relaxes the base SME step precisely because no single lane fits every document."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:163
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer's call after step 8. `iterate` returns to authoring with the feedback; `Authoring Committee feedback` sends a working draft to the committee through the Contributor Feedback sheet (Process_ContributorFeedback), and comes back to validation once its changes are merged; `approved` goes to publish."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Touched exactly once in this process — Task_SeedPlan turns the plan into a bean right after Task_Plan, so a resumed session or a sibling agent can pick the authoring loop up without re-deriving what was decided at the top."
msgstr ""

